                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "525445b4-baf0-3264-930d-a77412bfa1fd",
                                        "entry_id": "f079d859-69d2-3ac7-8db1-b561158b2c81",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see double, barrelled. Having two barrels, as a gun."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d74fa150-498c-3341-adab-b74819a27dc7",
                                        "entry_id": "f079d859-69d2-3ac7-8db1-b561158b2c81",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Twofold, having a double purpose or nature."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6ff53e1-2af7-4cf4-baee-2a6b2c70e07f",
                                                "sense_id": "d74fa150-498c-3341-adab-b74819a27dc7",
                                                "text": "Alexander Taylor, a native of Stonehaven who in the later forties went to Edinburgh, where he enjoyed a double-barrelled reputation as a rhymester and as an astronomer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78854539-43a2-469f-b519-3a32987a0d3a",
                                                "sense_id": "d74fa150-498c-3341-adab-b74819a27dc7",
                                                "text": "Order-maintenance crackdowns are not an alternative but rather an addition to the severe penalties that dominate criminal justice […] What we are left with today is a system of severe punishments for major offenders and severe treatments for minor offenders and ordinary citizens, especially minorities, a double-barreled approach with significant effects on large numbers of our citizenry."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4edb5df5-dde3-4310-ad02-fa4f46a432ca",
                                                "sense_id": "d74fa150-498c-3341-adab-b74819a27dc7",
                                                "text": "Skilling came to Enron with a double-barrelled reputation: on the one hand he was known to be a cold man with a taste for macho showing-off (Enron employees nicknamed him 'Darth Vader'). On the other hand he was said to be a genius ..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4014e561-f7d4-3e35-90b7-08ebbdb742a7",
                                        "entry_id": "f079d859-69d2-3ac7-8db1-b561158b2c81",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having two separate parts, often adjoined by a hyphen (or sometimes a space)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2a2b165-685b-403a-ae30-7bc77d2f09b7",
                                                "sense_id": "4014e561-f7d4-3e35-90b7-08ebbdb742a7",
                                                "text": "Almost unbelievably, some authors have formed the erroneous conception that ‘Hobson-Jobson’ is actually the double-barrelled surname of the dictionary’s editor."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0ced1fb1-c394-3ae3-b544-966629223f33",
                                        "entry_id": "f079d859-69d2-3ac7-8db1-b561158b2c81",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Forceful, powerful (like a double-barrelled shotgun)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b70764a1-5c6c-4b65-ad6f-beab4f7662a5",
                                                "sense_id": "0ced1fb1-c394-3ae3-b544-966629223f33",
                                                "text": "When the sheriff arrested [Lucy Hicks Anderson] one night, her double-barrelled reputation paid off—Charles Donlon, the town's leading banker, promptly bailed her out. Reason: He had scheduled a huge dinner party, which would have collapsed dismally with Lucy In gaol."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97b523a1-a59e-42ac-89e0-8be5db65d77a",
                                                "sense_id": "0ced1fb1-c394-3ae3-b544-966629223f33",
                                                "text": "Range Rover ran an ad campaign referring to grouse shooting with the line: “There’s only one car for the double-barrelled.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
